EOF
[?2004h> # Database Host Fix for Staging Web-API
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Problem
[?2004l[?2004h> `./render.py staging web-api` was returning `db-prod.internal` instead of `db-staging.internal`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Cause
[?2004l[?2004h> The config merge order in render.py is:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. base/defaults.yaml
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. environments/{environment}.yaml  
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. services/{service}.yaml
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. overrides/.legacy/{service}.yaml (legacy compatibility layer)
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. overrides/{environment}/{service}.yaml
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The legacy file `./overrides/.legacy/web-api.yaml` contains:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```yaml
[?2004l[?2004h> database:
[?2004l[?2004h>   host: db-prod.internal
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This was merged AFTER the staging environment config (which correctly set db-staging.internal)
[?2004l[?2004h> but BEFORE the staging override. Since the staging override didn't explicitly set database.host,
[?2004l[?2004h> the legacy value persisted.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Production worked because `./overrides/production/web-api.yaml` explicitly set the host,
[?2004l[?2004h> overriding the legacy value.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Solution
[?2004l[?2004h> Added `database.host: db-staging.internal` to `./overrides/staging/web-api.yaml`:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```yaml
[?2004l[?2004h> database:
[?2004l[?2004h>   host: db-staging.internal
[?2004l[?2004h>   pool_size: 15
[?2004l[?2004h> features:
[?2004l[?2004h>   debug_mode: true
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> - Staging now correctly renders: db-staging.internal ✓
[?2004l[?2004h> - Production still correctly renders: db-prod.internal ✓
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@41fb9ce0900b:/home/user/deploy# 